The T4 teardown order and the T5 counters are in the payload, quoted from it
(not from the commit):

```
5950		sm750_test_pattern_cancel(sdev);
5951		a65_mark("after test_pattern_cancel");
5952		a65_mark("before vblank_stop");
5953		sm750_vblank_timer_stop(sdev, true);
5954		a65_mark("after vblank_stop");
5955		/* 2. Shut the pipeline down while its buffer is still allocated. */
5956		a65_mark("before atomic_shutdown");
5957		drm_atomic_helper_shutdown(&sdev->drm);
5958		a65_mark("after atomic_shutdown");
...
5969		disable_work_sync(&sdev->mode_defer_work);
...
5971		sm750_destroy_shadow_workqueue(sdev);
5973		sm750_detach_vtconsole(sdev);
5974		a65_mark("before unplug");
5975		drm_dev_unplug(&sdev->drm);
5976		a65_mark("after unplug");
```

The shadow queue is destroyed at line 5971 while the buffer its worker reads is
still allocated, and the unplug at 5975 happens with no driver mutex held; the
blocking `mode_lock` paths in fbcon are gone from the same file
(`mutex_trylock(&sdev->mode_lock)` at lines 4323 and 4534), and the three
`WARN_ON(mutex_is_locked(...))` lines after the unplug are in the payload.

