## 7. what this install did not do

The reload. t7 was scoped to the install; `sm750-pkg reload`, `modprobe -r` and
`sm750-vt off` were forbidden in that session because the module refcount was 1
with two `/dev/dri/renderD128` descriptors held by the owner's browser. At the
time of the install the live module therefore still reported 0.6.10 and had no
`a65_trace` parameter and no `b8_*` attributes; that state is captured in
`/mega/tmp/sm750/t7/pre-install.txt` and `docs/evidence/runtime/56-dmesg-restrict-off.txt`
precedes it.

A reboot at 2026-11-28T07:52:12Z (not performed by this task) then loaded the
installed 0.6.11 tree, and the runtime evidence that had to be deferred is now
obtainable; it is recorded in `docs/evidence/runtime/57-instrumented-load.txt`.

