The first `make check` of this round, without the three libdrm variables, exited
2 in `check-deps`:

```
libdrm development files are required by tests/check-vblank.
  Debian/Ubuntu: sudo apt install libdrm-dev
  Fedora:        sudo dnf install libdrm-devel
  Rootless alternative: see docs/ENVIRONMENT.md
make: *** [Makefile:18: check-deps] Error 1
```

That is the preflight doing its job: `libdrm-devel` is absent from the rpmdb on
this host and `dnf install` by bare name is not allowlisted. The second run used
the rootless recipe of `docs/ENVIRONMENT.md` section 4 and exited 0. No check was
relaxed and no file was changed to get there.

The rpm-dkms gate's `SKIP` lines are its documented root-only tail: it rebuilds
the noarch RPM in a sandbox, asserts the payload against `git ls-files`, rejects
the eight planted controls, and skips the host install/erase, which sections 5
and 6 of this file cover with root through the allowlisted helper.
